berkeley-principles-4.logic.r3: argue/equivocates: P2 (S3): "perceive" is taken as immediately perceived, i.e. the direct content of sensing, which can only be our own ideas or sensations in P2 and as perceived through the senses, as ordinary objects like houses and rivers are, perhaps by means of sensations where perceived_by_sense is used else, a reader says: the argument holds only if they are one; taken apart, C (S2) does not follow (berkeley-principles-4.logic.r3.sense1)
